title: 'Decide: should Http stopped_p wait (bounded) for the session DELETE at daemon
  shutdown?'
updated: 2026-11-06T07:40:51Z
---

Split from k101 item 1. Since k94 a stop ends a Streamable HTTP session with one fire-and-forget DELETE. Http inherits a stopped_p that resolves at once, and the daemon exits soon after shutdown_p, so on shutdown the DELETE most likely never gets out (on a reload it does). Options: (a) leave it -- the remote times the session out; (b) Http::stopped_p waits for the DELETE, bounded by the connect/request timeout -- can delay shutdown by up to that timeout per dead remote (in parallel across upstreams). Maintainer decision.
